1401
01:01:53.120 --> 01:02:00.820
So I will say for me, I can go to a dinner party or a social interaction and on paper, everything
所以我想说，对我而言，我可以去参加晚宴或进行社交互动，从表面上看，一切

1402
01:02:00.820 --> 01:02:01.420
went great.
都进行得很顺利。

1403
01:02:01.680 --> 01:02:04.160
I always know what I'm going to get the next day with you.
我总是知道第二天会从你那里得到什么。

1404
01:02:04.160 --> 01:02:09.360
So I get a voicemail where you spiral.
我会收到你的语音留言，听着你陷入焦虑。

1405
01:02:10.020 --> 01:02:12.580
Yeah, it's really amazing.
是啊，这真的很神奇。

1406
01:02:12.800 --> 01:02:14.460
Actually, I can come home.
其实，我回到家后，

1407
01:02:14.560 --> 01:02:16.260
I will review every moment in my head.
会在脑海里复盘每一个瞬间。

1408
01:02:16.400 --> 01:02:20.700
I will think of all the ways I messed up, embarrassed myself, offended someone, my heart
我会想到所有我搞砸了、让自己尴尬、冒犯了别人的地方，我的心

1409
01:02:20.700 --> 01:02:21.240
will race.
会狂跳不止。

1410
01:02:21.500 --> 01:02:24.140
I will lose sleep, sometimes for days.
我会失眠，有时甚至会持续好几天。

1411
01:02:24.620 --> 01:02:27.620
And this has been going on for me for as long as I can remember.
这种情况从我记事起就一直伴随着我。

1412
01:02:27.780 --> 01:02:29.120
I have always had this.
我一直都有这个问题。

1413
01:02:29.560 --> 01:02:32.140
I've gone to therapy for it, which has helped a ton.
我为此接受过心理治疗，这对我帮助很大。

1414
01:02:32.140 --> 01:02:36.180
And I did that therapy before I became a professional actor.
而且我在成为职业演员之前就做过心理治疗了。

1415
01:02:36.340 --> 01:02:38.180
So I'm very grateful for that.
所以我对此非常感激。

1416
01:02:38.340 --> 01:02:40.680
I started therapy in my early 20s.
我在20岁出头时就开始接受心理治疗了。

1417
01:02:41.740 --> 01:02:47.780
But I have to say, Anouk, in answer to your question, acting has always been a little bit
但我必须说，阿努克，回答你的问题，表演对我来说一直以来

1418
01:02:47.780 --> 01:02:48.760
of an escape for me.
都是一种逃避方式。

1419
01:02:49.380 --> 01:02:52.160
In high school, like I said, I would avoid going to parties.
就像我说的，在高中时，我会避免去参加派对。

1420
01:02:52.740 --> 01:02:55.340
But I loved being part of theater productions.
但我喜欢参与戏剧制作。

1421
01:02:55.780 --> 01:02:57.560
I loved the artistic community.
我喜欢那个艺术社区。

1422
01:02:57.840 --> 01:02:59.240
I felt safe there.
我在那里感到安全。

1423
01:02:59.400 --> 01:03:01.320
It's a very accepting group of folks.
那是一群非常包容的人。

1424
01:03:01.320 --> 01:03:02.120
It is.
确实如此。

1425
01:03:02.240 --> 01:03:07.320
And I often do well socially when there's a project involved, when we all have something
当有项目参与其中，当我们都有共同的目标或努力方向时，

1426
01:03:07.320 --> 01:03:09.060
we're working on or working toward.
我在社交方面通常表现得不错。

1427
01:03:09.700 --> 01:03:13.220
Because I do like people, and I like being around people.
因为我确实喜欢人，也喜欢和人待在一起。

1428
01:03:13.420 --> 01:03:16.260
And you're goal-oriented, so it's like you have that common goal.
而且你目标导向很强，所以就像你们有了共同的目标一样。

1429
01:03:16.540 --> 01:03:23.240
So while I love acting, the part that has been hardest for me has been the public events
所以虽然我热爱表演，但对我来说最困难的部分一直是公共活动，

1430
01:03:23.240 --> 01:03:28.800
like interviews or red carpets, things like that.
比如采访或红毯之类的场合。

1431
01:03:28.800 --> 01:03:34.660
But I wrote in our book, The Office BFFs, that Melora, who plays Jan, was a really great
但我曾在我们的书《办公室闺蜜》中写道，饰演简的梅洛拉，

1432
01:03:34.660 --> 01:03:39.700
mentor for me and how to navigate that part of the business with boundaries and self-care.
是我在如何通过界限感和自我关怀来应对这部分业务方面的良师益友。

1433
01:03:40.240 --> 01:03:44.540
You know, it just requires a lot of thought, a lot of strategy for me.
你知道，这对我来说需要深思熟虑，需要很多策略。

1434
01:03:45.000 --> 01:03:48.260
But yeah, this anxiety has never gone away.
但没错，这种焦虑从未消失。

1435
01:03:48.440 --> 01:03:50.240
It just ebbs and flows.
它只是时起时伏。

1436
01:03:50.240 --> 01:03:52.580
But here you are, crushing it, lady.
但你现在做得非常出色，女士。

1437
01:03:52.780 --> 01:03:53.300
Here I am.
我确实在这里。

1438
01:03:53.360 --> 01:03:55.620
Listen, like you said, I'm also very stubborn.
听着，就像你说的，我也很固执。

1439
01:03:55.800 --> 01:03:56.860
I don't like to be stopped.
我不喜欢被阻挡。

1440
01:03:57.160 --> 01:04:04.040
So I am a stubborn social introvert with social anxiety and an actor and a podcaster.
所以我是一个固执的社交内向者，患有社交焦虑，同时也是一名演员和播客主持人。

1441
01:04:04.320 --> 01:04:05.600
And a mom and a friend.
还是一位母亲和朋友。

1442
01:04:05.820 --> 01:04:11.940
And I have the best BFF because having someone who will listen to me spiral the morning after
而且我有最好的闺蜜，因为有人愿意听我在晚宴后的第二天早上陷入焦虑，

1443
01:04:11.940 --> 01:04:14.800
a dinner party, that helps a lot.
这真的很有帮助。

1444
01:04:14.800 --> 01:04:16.840
So thank you, lady, for being there for me.
所以谢谢你，女士，一直陪伴着我。

1445
01:04:17.240 --> 01:04:18.040
I always will.
我永远都会在。

1446
01:04:18.700 --> 01:04:22.400
Now, Angela Anuk also had a question for you, which is this.
现在，安吉拉，阿努克也有一个问题要问你，是这样的。

1447
01:04:22.840 --> 01:04:25.860
I know that Angela has shared that she grew up in Indonesia.
我知道安吉拉分享过她是在印度尼西亚长大的。

1448
01:04:26.140 --> 01:04:32.160
And as a TCK myself, I was wondering if she could share some of her experiences and difficulties
作为一名第三文化小孩（TCK），我想知道她能否分享一些她在那里成长的经历和困难，

1449
01:04:32.160 --> 01:04:36.100
in growing up there and what it was like returning to the U.S.
以及回到美国是什么感觉，

1450
01:04:36.200 --> 01:04:39.060
and if and how it has affected her identity.
以及这是否影响了她的身份认同，又是如何影响的。

1451
01:04:39.440 --> 01:04:40.240
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1452
01:04:40.500 --> 01:04:44.680
Anuk, first of all, I think I went into comedy because we move so much.
Anuk，首先，我想我之所以走上喜剧这条路，是因为我们搬家太频繁了。

1453
01:04:44.800 --> 01:04:46.780
And I was such a fish out of water growing up.
我在成长过程中总是感到格格不入。

1454
01:04:46.900 --> 01:04:51.720
And the quickest way for me to fit in was to make everyone laugh.
而让我融入环境最快的方式就是逗大家笑。

1455
01:04:52.100 --> 01:04:55.240
But TCK means a third cultural kid.
TCK 指的是“第三文化小孩”。

1456
01:04:55.860 --> 01:04:58.660
And you grow up not in your home country.
你在非母国的环境中长大。

1457
01:04:59.160 --> 01:05:03.560
And you have a hard time kind of figuring out where you fit in.
你会很难找到自己的归属感。

1458
01:05:03.680 --> 01:05:09.120
Because there's a huge part of me that loves and identifies with my childhood in Jakarta.
因为我内心深处非常热爱并认同我在雅加达的童年时光。

1459
01:05:09.120 --> 01:05:16.160
And when I came to the U.S., I found it hard to fit in and find other people who had had an experience like that.
当我来到美国时，我发现很难融入，也很难找到有类似经历的人。

1460
01:05:17.660 --> 01:05:23.020
But yet my family, my parents who were raising me in this other country,
但我的家人，也就是在那个异国他乡抚养我长大的父母，

1461
01:05:23.300 --> 01:05:26.980
had all of their traditions from their culture and where they grew up.
他们保留着自己文化和成长背景中的所有传统。

1462
01:05:26.980 --> 01:05:34.040
And when I would go to Texas and Louisiana in the summers and I wouldn't understand pop cultural references
每当夏天我去德克萨斯州和路易斯安那州时，我听不懂那里的流行文化梗，

1463
01:05:34.040 --> 01:05:39.600
or I wouldn't understand colloquialisms or I felt like out of place there too.
也不懂当地的俗语，在那儿我也感到格格不入。

1464
01:05:39.840 --> 01:05:42.140
And it was sort of like, where do I fit in?
当时我就在想，我到底属于哪里？

1465
01:05:42.340 --> 01:05:48.620
And then you have this small group of people who also grew up like you that you really hold tight and dear.
然后你会遇到一小群和你成长背景相似的人，你会非常珍惜他们。

1466
01:05:48.620 --> 01:05:52.820
I am still friends with my friends that I grew up with in Jakarta.
我和在雅加达一起长大的朋友至今仍保持着联系。

1467
01:05:53.060 --> 01:05:54.960
We all moved and got dispersed.
我们后来都搬走了，散落在各地。

1468
01:05:55.250 --> 01:05:56.760
And that's another thing.
这也是一个问题。

1469
01:05:56.940 --> 01:06:03.700
Because you don't have that constant touchstone of that neighborhood you always go home to,
因为你没有那种可以随时回去的、恒定的社区归属感，

1470
01:06:03.980 --> 01:06:07.600
that corner store, that coffee shop.
没有那个转角的杂货店，没有那家咖啡馆。

1471
01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:10.440
You grow up kind of displaced a little bit.
你在成长过程中多少会感到有些漂泊不定。

1472
01:06:10.940 --> 01:06:14.200
And it makes me crave roots and tradition.
这让我非常渴望扎根和传统。

1473
01:06:14.660 --> 01:06:18.520
I get very attached to the smallest things about family tradition.
我对家庭传统中哪怕最细微的事情都非常执着。

1474
01:06:18.740 --> 01:06:19.820
Like, okay, it's Christmas Eve.
比如，好吧，现在是平安夜。

1475
01:06:19.820 --> 01:06:21.480
We open one gift on Christmas Eve.
我们平安夜拆一份礼物。

1476
01:06:21.640 --> 01:06:24.780
And I remember one year my mom was like, what if we just open all of them?
我记得有一年我妈说，要不我们把礼物全拆了吧？

1477
01:06:24.880 --> 01:06:25.680
And I was like, no!
我当时就说，不行！

1478
01:06:26.400 --> 01:06:29.420
Because I needed some type of roots.
因为我需要某种形式的根基。

1479
01:06:31.220 --> 01:06:36.100
But I am thankful for my childhood because I really believe, and I know this,
但我很感激我的童年，因为我坚信，而且我知道，

1480
01:06:36.300 --> 01:06:40.180
that you could drop me anywhere and I will find a way to survive.
无论把我扔到哪里，我都能找到生存之道。

1481
01:06:40.180 --> 01:06:41.320
I'll find my people.
我能找到志同道合的人。

1482
01:06:41.320 --> 01:06:43.640
I'll find out what to do there.
我能弄清楚该做什么。

1483
01:06:43.780 --> 01:06:44.360
And I'll be okay.
我会过得很好。

1484
01:06:45.380 --> 01:06:45.600
Yeah.
是的。

1485
01:06:45.720 --> 01:06:51.500
I'm not fearful at all about new places and new experiences and new people and new cultures.
我对新地方、新体验、新人群和新文化一点也不感到恐惧。

1486
01:06:51.720 --> 01:06:53.400
I get excited about it.
我反而感到很兴奋。

1487
01:06:53.540 --> 01:06:53.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1488
01:06:54.440 --> 01:06:57.400
But yeah, Anouk, I can definitely relate to that.
但确实，Anouk，我对此深有同感。

1489
01:06:57.580 --> 01:07:01.240
And ultimately now, as an adult, I see it as a gift.
最终，作为成年人，我现在把它视为一种天赋。

1490
01:07:01.240 --> 01:07:04.880
But when I was a kid and we moved back in middle school, that was a tough time.
但当我还是个孩子，在初中时搬回国，那段日子真的很难熬。

1491
01:07:05.100 --> 01:07:06.740
And middle school is already tough.
初中本来就很难熬。

1492
01:07:06.860 --> 01:07:07.480
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1493
01:07:07.480 --> 01:07:08.320
It's like, what?
就像是，什么情况？

1494
01:07:08.460 --> 01:07:09.820
Am I wearing a training bra?
我是不是在穿发育内衣？

1495
01:07:09.820 --> 01:07:11.600
Oh, what's happening?
哦，发生了什么？

1496
01:07:12.000 --> 01:07:15.300
The most miserable couple years of my life for middle school.
初中是我人生中最痛苦的几年。

1497
01:07:15.320 --> 01:07:15.820
I know.
我懂的。

1498
01:07:16.000 --> 01:07:17.580
And I can still feel them.
那种感觉我至今记忆犹新。

1499
01:07:17.840 --> 01:07:25.780
So for you to be also new, not just new school or new kid, but like new to being back in the country.
所以对你来说，不仅是转学或成为新同学，更是重新适应这个国家，那种感觉一定更强烈。

1500
01:07:26.000 --> 01:07:26.320
Yeah.
是的。

1501
01:07:26.580 --> 01:07:26.840
Wow.
哇。

1502
01:07:26.840 --> 01:07:26.890
Wow.
哇。

1503
01:07:27.480 --> 01:07:28.000
I know.
我知道。

1504
01:07:28.140 --> 01:07:31.120
I would say things, too, and people would be like, what are you talking about?
我以前也会说些什么，然后人们就会问，你在说什么呢？

1505
01:07:31.280 --> 01:07:31.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1506
01:07:31.820 --> 01:07:32.480
All the time.
一直都是这样。

1507
01:07:32.780 --> 01:07:34.940
But Anouk, thanks so much for asking about that.
不过Anouk，非常感谢你问起这件事。

1508
01:07:35.040 --> 01:07:37.280
It's a part of my childhood that I just treasure.
这是我童年里非常珍视的一部分。

1509
01:07:37.680 --> 01:07:43.700
As an adult, I really have seen it now to be such a gift that I had, that I grew up in a different country.
成年后，我真的觉得在不同的国家长大是一份礼物。

1510
01:07:43.700 --> 01:07:50.240
I have such great perspective and appreciation for sort of a global view of the world, that we're all in this together.
我对世界有了很好的视角和认识，意识到我们都是命运共同体。

1511
01:07:50.240 --> 01:07:51.220
We really are.
确实如此。

1512
01:07:51.640 --> 01:07:54.220
So I love it when people reach out to me about that.
所以我很喜欢人们就此与我交流。

1513
01:07:54.440 --> 01:08:00.480
I also got a letter from Sarah, who is living near my old school in South Jakarta.
我还收到了一封来自Sarah的信，她住在我在南雅加达的老学校附近。

1514
01:08:00.480 --> 01:08:01.220
No way.
不会吧。

1515
01:08:01.400 --> 01:08:01.540
Yeah.
是的。

1516
01:08:01.660 --> 01:08:04.240
She's living near JIS, which is where I went to school.
她住在JIS附近，那是我以前上学的地方。

1517
01:08:04.720 --> 01:08:08.600
And she sent me the most beautiful batik skirt.
她还送了我一条最漂亮的蜡染裙子。

1518
01:08:09.060 --> 01:08:10.580
Sarah, I'm totally going to wear it.
Sarah，我一定会穿它的。

1519
01:08:10.660 --> 01:08:11.380
It's so beautiful.
它太美了。

1520
01:08:11.380 --> 01:08:13.000
I'll put a photo of it in stories.
我会把照片发到快拍里。

1521
01:08:13.480 --> 01:08:14.780
Here's the letter she wrote.
这是她写的信。

1522
01:08:15.200 --> 01:08:18.860
Dear office ladies, my family and I have been huge office fans.
亲爱的办公室女士们，我和我的家人一直是《办公室》的忠实粉丝。

1523
01:08:19.020 --> 01:08:21.220
And so when your podcast came out, I was thrilled.
所以当你们的播客上线时，我非常激动。

1524
01:08:21.700 --> 01:08:25.460
And imagine our delight to find out that Angela went to school at JIS.
想象一下，当我们发现Angela曾在JIS上学时有多开心。

1525
01:08:25.820 --> 01:08:29.240
We have lived down the street from that school for the last five years.
过去五年里，我们就住在离那所学校不远的街上。

1526
01:08:29.240 --> 01:08:37.780
And I just had to reach out and send you guys a few goodies, a traditional batik skirt and Javanese coffee from Luwak.
我一定要联系你们，给你们寄点小礼物，一条传统的蜡染裙子和来自Luwak的爪哇咖啡。

1527
01:08:38.020 --> 01:08:39.580
Jenna, you would love this coffee.
Jenna，你一定会喜欢这种咖啡的。

1528
01:08:39.860 --> 01:08:41.020
You know I love a coffee.
你知道我喜欢喝咖啡。

1529
01:08:41.040 --> 01:08:41.620
I know.
我知道。

1530
01:08:42.220 --> 01:08:44.280
Please keep up the great work on the podcaSt.
请继续保持播客的高水准。

1531
01:08:44.300 --> 01:08:48.320
So great to enjoy a bit of home when abroad with much love.
在国外能享受到一点家乡的味道真是太棒了，爱你们。

1532
01:08:48.620 --> 01:08:49.060
Sarah.
Sarah。

1533
01:08:49.600 --> 01:08:50.880
Sarah, thank you.
Sarah，谢谢你。

1534
01:08:51.880 --> 01:08:53.440
I just said thank you, Sarah.
我刚才已经说谢谢Sarah了。

1535
01:08:54.540 --> 01:08:56.820
Well, I love when people send us things, Angela.
嗯，我喜欢人们给我们寄东西，Angela。

1536
01:08:56.820 --> 01:09:00.820
And people get real creative in the things they send.
而且人们寄来的东西真的很有创意。

1537
01:09:01.200 --> 01:09:03.560
I got a letter from Chris S.
我收到了一封来自田纳西州诺克斯维尔的Chris S.的信。

1538
01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:09.460
in Knoxville, Tennessee, who remembered when we talked about our love of Wheel of Fortune.
他记得我们聊过对《幸运轮》节目的喜爱。

1539
01:09:09.740 --> 01:09:11.480
Oh, my grandmother's favorite show.
哦，那是我祖母最喜欢的节目。

1540
01:09:11.820 --> 01:09:16.680
Chris emailed Vanna White and told her that we were fans.
Chris给Vanna White发了邮件，告诉她我们是粉丝。

1541
01:09:17.440 --> 01:09:26.860
I don't know how he had her email, but somehow he got her to send us each personalized photos autographed by Vanna White and Pat Sajak.
我不知道他是怎么弄到她邮箱的，但他不知怎么就让她给我们每人寄来了Vanna White和Pat Sajak亲笔签名的个人照片。

1542
01:09:26.980 --> 01:09:27.620
Here they are.
就在这儿。

1543
01:09:27.740 --> 01:09:28.360
You are kidding me.
你在开玩笑吧。

1544
01:09:29.000 --> 01:09:31.480
Somewhere my grandmother in heaven is smiling.
在天堂的祖母一定在微笑。

1545
01:09:32.240 --> 01:09:33.640
Wait, I have to see this.
等等，我得看看。

1546
01:09:33.700 --> 01:09:35.200
Here, there's one for each of us.
给你，我们每人一张。

1547
01:09:35.300 --> 01:09:35.800
There it is.
在这儿呢。

1548
01:09:36.060 --> 01:09:38.040
To Angela Hart Vanna White.
致Angela Hart，Vanna White。

1549
01:09:38.180 --> 01:09:38.740
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1550
01:09:38.800 --> 01:09:39.580
And Pat Sajak.
还有Pat Sajak。

1551
01:09:39.680 --> 01:09:40.640
And Pat Sajak.
还有帕特·萨杰。

1552
01:09:41.280 --> 01:09:42.560
Look how glamorous.
看，多迷人啊。

1553
01:09:42.940 --> 01:09:44.320
Look how glamorous she looks.
看她看起来多迷人。

1554
01:09:44.340 --> 01:09:45.020
It's a great photo.
这照片真棒。

1555
01:09:45.280 --> 01:09:46.040
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1556
01:09:46.460 --> 01:09:47.860
That is amazing.
太惊人了。

1557
01:09:48.240 --> 01:09:50.460
Angela, when we get our new studio space.
安吉拉，等我们有了新的工作室空间。

1558
01:09:50.460 --> 01:09:51.500
That's going up on the wall.
那张照片要挂在墙上。

1559
01:09:51.500 --> 01:09:55.460
We're going to have the best autograph wall, thanks to Sam and Chris.
多亏了山姆和克里斯，我们将拥有最棒的签名墙。

1560
01:09:55.760 --> 01:10:00.040
And my God, if we could get a personalized autograph from Keanu.
天哪，如果我们能得到基努的亲笔签名就好了。

1561
01:10:00.040 --> 01:10:00.520
Don't say it.
别说了。

1562
01:10:00.600 --> 01:10:01.540
Don't even say it.
提都别提。

1563
01:10:01.640 --> 01:10:02.160
From Keanu.
基努的签名。

1564
01:10:02.160 --> 01:10:03.120
Don't even say it.
提都别提。

1565
01:10:03.200 --> 01:10:05.340
The wall will be complete.
那这面墙就圆满了。

1566
01:10:06.700 --> 01:10:07.520
Keanu, please.
基努，拜托了。

1567
01:10:10.250 --> 01:10:11.050
A great space.
一个很棒的空间。

1568
01:10:11.550 --> 01:10:12.710
And you'll love it.
你会喜欢的。

1569
01:10:12.710 --> 01:10:13.670
Keanu, please.
基努，拜托了。

1570
01:10:13.850 --> 01:10:14.550
We're just saying.
我们只是随口说说。

1571
01:10:15.010 --> 01:10:16.970
We also love getting your art.
我们也喜欢收到你们的艺术作品。

1572
01:10:17.150 --> 01:10:20.090
So many of you guys have painted and drawn pictures for us.
你们中有很多人为我们画了画。

1573
01:10:20.250 --> 01:10:22.130
That's going to go on our wall in our new space.
那些画会挂在我们新空间的墙上。

1574
01:10:22.270 --> 01:10:22.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1575
01:10:22.830 --> 01:10:28.530
I want to give a shout out to the coolest art sent in by unluckypress.com.
我要特别感谢 unluckypress.com 寄来的最酷的艺术品。

1576
01:10:28.850 --> 01:10:29.850
It's so great.
太棒了。

1577
01:10:30.270 --> 01:10:31.250
It's, okay, guys.
好了，伙计们。

1578
01:10:32.090 --> 01:10:36.650
Imagine the Charles Schultz Peanuts Gang meets Cafe Disco.
想象一下《花生漫画》里的角色来到了“咖啡迪斯科”。

1579
01:10:36.850 --> 01:10:37.210
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1580
01:10:37.210 --> 01:10:43.110
It's the whole kind of hangout down in Cafe Disco portrayed by the Peanuts characters.
就是整个“咖啡迪斯科”的聚会场景，由《花生漫画》的角色来演绎。

1581
01:10:43.370 --> 01:10:46.170
But it's like a Peanuts Pam and a Peanuts Angela.
就像是《花生》版的帕姆和《花生》版的安吉拉。

1582
01:10:46.370 --> 01:10:47.250
Yes, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1583
01:10:47.430 --> 01:10:47.650
Right?
对吧？

1584
01:10:47.930 --> 01:10:48.130
Yes.
是的。

1585
01:10:48.130 --> 01:10:50.030
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

1586
01:10:50.250 --> 01:10:51.590
It's so stinking cute.
简直可爱得不得了。

1587
01:10:51.710 --> 01:10:53.290
We're going to put it in our Instagram.
我们要把它发到我们的 Instagram 上。

1588
01:10:53.430 --> 01:10:54.910
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

1589
01:10:55.130 --> 01:10:56.870
I have another fun thing to share.
我还有一件有趣的事要分享。

1590
01:10:57.090 --> 01:10:57.990
What is it?
是什么？

1591
01:10:57.990 --> 01:11:04.370
I got a birthday card from Catherine in Lincoln, Nebraska, and she put a business card inside
我收到了内布拉斯加州林肯市凯瑟琳寄来的生日贺卡，她在里面放了一张名片

1592
01:11:04.370 --> 01:11:05.210
with a note.
还有一张便条。

1593
01:11:05.650 --> 01:11:07.910
I am fascinated by her business card.
我对她的名片很感兴趣。

1594
01:11:08.070 --> 01:11:08.470
What is it?
是什么？

1595
01:11:08.470 --> 01:11:10.390
I did a deep dive on her business card.
我深入研究了一下她的名片。

1596
01:11:10.450 --> 01:11:11.190
What is it?
是什么？

1597
01:11:11.330 --> 01:11:15.050
It said, quote, blank journals and more.
上面写着，引用一下，“空白日志及更多”。

1598
01:11:15.670 --> 01:11:18.010
Lady, she makes her own journals.
天哪，她自己制作日志本。

1599
01:11:18.410 --> 01:11:19.490
You're kidding me.
你开玩笑吧。

1600
01:11:19.610 --> 01:11:22.590
I found a write-up about Catherine, and here's something she said.
我找到了一篇关于凯瑟琳的报道，这是她说的一段话。

1601
01:11:23.170 --> 01:11:25.070
Bookbinding has become my passion.
装帧艺术已经成了我的挚爱。

1602
01:11:25.070 --> 01:11:30.990
Out of a love for beautiful and unique papers, leathers, beads, and other found objects that
出于对精美独特的纸张、皮革、珠子以及其他我从日常生活中收集到的物件的喜爱，

1603
01:11:30.990 --> 01:11:32.790
I collect from my everyday life.
我收集了这些东西。

1604
01:11:32.930 --> 01:11:38.190
By combining these different elements, I create each book as an individual piece of art.
通过将这些不同的元素结合起来，我把每一本书都创作成了独立的艺术品。

1605
01:11:38.690 --> 01:11:41.190
They each have a title, a theme, and a voice.
它们每一本都有自己的标题、主题和灵魂。

1606
01:11:41.450 --> 01:11:46.290
Each book is full of blank pages for use as a journal, a photo album, a sketchbook, or
每一本书里都装满了空白页，可以用作日记本、相册、素描本，或者

1607
01:11:46.290 --> 01:11:48.530
simply a personal place to put thoughts.
仅仅是一个存放个人思绪的私密空间。

1608
01:11:48.990 --> 01:11:54.450
She has a studio in her home where she fulfills custom orders, and she currently teaches and
她在家里有一间工作室，专门处理定制订单，目前她也在各地教授和

1609
01:11:54.450 --> 01:11:57.050
demonstrates paper arts at various locations.
演示纸艺。

1610
01:11:57.490 --> 01:11:59.690
Catherine, I found you on Etsy.
凯瑟琳，我是在Etsy上发现你的。

1611
01:11:59.890 --> 01:12:01.190
Your journals are beautiful.
你的手账本太美了。

1612
01:12:01.430 --> 01:12:05.510
I saw you're taking some time off, but when you're back, I will be ordering one.
我看到你最近在休息，但等你回来，我一定会订购一本。

1613
01:12:06.050 --> 01:12:07.810
Angela, yes, you will be.
安吉拉，没错，你一定会订的。

1614
01:12:07.970 --> 01:12:08.610
I know.
我知道。

1615
01:12:08.750 --> 01:12:14.230
I can't wait to write ridiculously stupid things in it, but it will be mine, and it will
我迫不及待想在里面写些荒唐愚蠢的东西，但它会是属于我的，而且它会

1616
01:12:14.230 --> 01:12:14.890
be beautiful.
非常漂亮。

1617
01:12:15.370 --> 01:12:19.250
Well, guys, thank you for all of your mail.
好了，伙计们，谢谢你们寄来的所有邮件。

1618
01:12:19.250 --> 01:12:24.290
I really felt like I spent the last few days with you guys, just hearing your voices, hearing
我真的感觉过去几天是和你们一起度过的，听着你们的声音，听着

1619
01:12:24.290 --> 01:12:26.770
your stories, and it really built me up.
你们的故事，这真的让我深受鼓舞。

1620
01:12:26.950 --> 01:12:27.970
So thank you so much.
所以非常感谢你们。

1621
01:12:28.150 --> 01:12:31.190
We hope you have a wonderful holiday and a happy new year.
祝大家节日快乐，新年快乐。

